  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following compounds will undergo self aldol condensation in the presence of cold dilute alkali?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "j2grw",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_2=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CHO}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cEM8S",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH} \\equiv \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{CHO}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bBI6D",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{CHO}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1Dqit",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{CHO}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Aldehydes which contain $\\alpha$-hydrogen on a saturated carbon, i.e. $\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{CHO}$ will undergo aldol condensation.\nAlthough $\\mathrm{CH}_2=\\stackrel{\\alpha}{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{CHO}$ also contain a $\\alpha$-hydrogen atom but cannot be easily abstracted by a base to form a carbanion and hence does not undergo aldol condensation.",
    "image": null
  },
